.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFY 1 "October 2026" "plugin-qualify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualify \- find out whether an audio plugin is safe to run in a real-time audio engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualify
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIuri\fR|\fIbundle-path\fR...
.br
.B plugin-qualify
[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-\-all\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans each plugin, measures its latency and CPU cost per sample rate and buffer size, runs it under
a real host with memory checking, and prints one verdict per plugin: suitable, conditional, unknown
or unsuitable. A plugin that was not measured is never rated suitable.
A target is a plugin URI or an LV2 bundle (every plugin in it).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Every CLAP plugin on the CLAP search path: the directories CLAP_PATH names, then ~/.clap, then /usr/lib/clap.
LV2 plugins are not measured from this entry point, so when any LV2 bundle is on the LV2 path (LV2_PATH,
else ~/.lv2 and the system lv2 directories) the run refuses with exit 2 instead of qualifying only the CLAP side.
.TP
.BI \-\-rates " list"
Sample rates to measure at, comma-separated (default 44100,48000,96000,192000).
.TP
.BI \-\-quanta " list"
Buffer sizes in frames to rate cost at, comma-separated (default 128,256,512,1024).
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Write one JSON measurement document per run into this directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " json|text"
The verdicts as JSON, or as text (default).
.TP
.B \-\-isolate
Measure each plugin in a fresh worker, so a crash or hang takes only that plugin.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-host\-sweep
Offline measurement only, without mod-host.
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-profile " file|id"
Judge against this host: openmixer-console (default), jalv, mod-host, or a profile JSON file.
Repeat or comma-separate for one verdict per profile.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 every plugin qualified, 1 some did not, 2 something could not be measured.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/FreeMixer/plugin-qualify
